      ":question/id": "4471c240-666f-5f09-bee5-21fd864bc0e3",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $BC-BA$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nFill in the missing entries.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$BC-BA=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$-6$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$2$</td><td>$-1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$2$</td><td>$-3$</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Keep the common factor $B$ on the left and preserve the order of the subtraction:\n\n$$\nBC-BA=B(C-A).\n$$\n\nCombine corresponding entries first:\n\n$$\nC-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse row-by-column multiplication on the shorter product $B(C-A)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(BC-BA)_{12}&=(-3)(-1)+(2)(-1)=1 \\\\ (BC-BA)_{11}&=(2)(1)+(-3)(-1)=5 \\\\ (BC-BA)_{21}&=(-3)(1)+(-2)(-1)=-1 \\\\ (BC-BA)_{33}&=(1)(1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nBC-BA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"
    }
