      ":question/id": "680fddfd-6ede-51c4-9581-cb5528ee6a34",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $CA-BA$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nFill in the missing entries.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$CA-BA=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$1$</td><td>$-3$</td><td>$4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$4$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Keep the common factor $A$ on the right and preserve the order of the subtraction:\n\n$$\nCA-BA=(C-B)A.\n$$\n\nCombine corresponding entries first:\n\n$$\nC-B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse row-by-column multiplication on the shorter product $(C-B)A$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(CA-BA)_{13}&=(1)(-3)+(1)(-3)=-6 \\\\ (CA-BA)_{11}&=(1)(-2)+(1)(2)=0 \\\\ (CA-BA)_{32}&=(1)(-3)=-3 \\\\ (CA-BA)_{31}&=(-1)(-2)+(1)(3)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nCA-BA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"
    }
  },
