      ":question/problem": "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nFill in the missing entries.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB+AC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$1$</td><td>$-4$</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Keep the common factor $A$ on the left and preserve the order of the addition:\n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nCombine corresponding entries first:\n\n$$\nB+C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse row-by-column multiplication on the shorter product $A(B+C)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(AB+AC)_{23}&=(-1)(1)+(2)(-1)=-3 \\\\ (AB+AC)_{22}&=(2)(-1)+(2)(1)=0 \\\\ (AB+AC)_{11}&=(2)(-1)+(-1)(-1)=-1 \\\\ (AB+AC)_{13}&=(-1)(1)+(1)(-1)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nAB+AC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"
    }
  }
